  "step_2": "The individual states that Lottery A appears more lucrative than Lottery B because it has an 80% chance of winning 4000€ versus B's guaranteed 3000€. The individual does not mention skewness, risk, or any consideration of unfavorable outcomes. The justification is based solely on the perceived higher expected value or higher chance of a large reward. The deliberation process centers on the attractiveness of the 80% chance of winning 4000€, not on the distribution of probabilities in terms of skewness. There is no reference to unfavorable outcomes or the structure of probability in terms of skewness. Thus, the individual’s reasoning is based on expected value or perceived risk preference, not on skewness as defined in the decision reason.",
  "step_3": "The decision reason is not applicable to the lotteries because neither is right-skewed — in fact, A is left-skewed and B is not skewed. The individual did not consider skewness at all; instead, they evaluated the lotteries based on the likelihood of a large reward. Since the reason requires evaluating and preferring the more right-skewed lottery, and no such skewness exists, and the individual did not reference skewness in their reasoning, the decision reason was not used. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason to make the decision.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
