  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — that Lottery B has a higher probability (55%) of an unfavorable outcome (0 Euros) compared to Lottery A (10%), making B more right-skewed — is not mentioned or considered in the verbal report. The individual does not refer to skewness, nor does the individual evaluate the distribution of probabilities in terms of unfavorable outcomes. Instead, the justification is based on the potential for a larger gain and risk-taking, not on the skewness of the lotteries. Therefore, the decision reason (preferring the more right-skewed lottery) was not used in the deliberation process. The individual did not consider or apply the skewness-based rule to make the choice.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
